# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Several tests in src/__tests__ read application source as text and match
# against literals containing "\n" — tenantRlsFlag.test.js and the tenant
# convention tests, among others. Under the default Windows behaviour
# (core.autocrlf=true, which this machine has set), a checkout rewrites those
# files to CRLF, every "\n" literal stops matching, and the tests fail on a
# developer's machine while passing in Linux CI. That is the worst failure
# mode available: red locally, green in CI, so the local red gets ignored —
# and these are the tests guarding the tenant boundary during the RLS rollout.
#
# Fixing the tests to tolerate both line endings treats the symptom; the files
# themselves should simply be LF everywhere, which is what they are in the
# repository already.
#
# After adding this file, renormalise the existing working tree once:
#   git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary content must never be touched by the above.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.xlsx   binary
